    {
      "id": "0Z-0sgzO6bf4A-RNije_d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1812.4732536859656,
      "y": 1362.218745345624,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 165,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "iqRXNdub-whBvdO4OtSPZ"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3tz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1476803197,
      "version": 281,
      "versionNonce": 1038773220,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794665975962,
      "created": 1794643387444,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "VIEW FEED (READ PATH)\n1) User ID from JWT; validate limit / cursor.\n2) Read timeline post IDs from Redis sorted set.\n3) On cache miss, read durable FeedEntries.\n4) Merge hot-author + recommended candidates.\n5) Dedupe; filter visibility; batch hydrate posts.\n6) Return items + opaque next_cursor.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "VIEW FEED (READ PATH)\n1) User ID from JWT; validate limit / cursor.\n2) Read timeline post IDs from Redis sorted set.\n3) On cache miss, read durable FeedEntries.\n4) Merge hot-author + recommended candidates.\n5) Dedupe; filter visibility; batch hydrate posts.\n6) Return items + opaque next_cursor.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5v7p5TBK3fA7m5xh7vJCS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2279.065395689682,
      "y": 799.4554222962164,
      "width": 810,
      "height": 1150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4A",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 839638077,
      "version": 1916,
      "versionNonce": 1026405468,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794665975962,
      "created": 1794644212389,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HIGH LEVEL DESIGN — CORRECTED\n\nSTORAGE AND CONSISTENCY\n- PostgreSQL source of truth for Posts + Follows.\n- Create post + outbox event in ONE DB transaction.\n- Outbox publisher retries sending to Kafka.\n- Timeline delivery is async / eventually consistent.\n- 99.99% availability is a target, not a DB switch.\n- Primary failover needs fencing; replicas may lag.\n- Backups / restore + multi-AZ replication matter.\n\nCAPACITY ESTIMATES (ASSUMPTIONS)\n- 100M DAU x 10 reads/day = 1B feed reads/day.\n  Average 11,574 RPS; 10x peak 115,741 RPS.\n- 10M posts/day = 116 write RPS; peak ~1,157.\n- 10M posts x 500 bytes = ~5 GB raw/day;\n  ~1.8 TB/year excluding indexes/replicas/media.\n- Full fan-out x 500 followers => 5B timeline\n  entry writes/day (~57.9k average writes/sec).\n\nSERVING PATH\n- Posts index by (author_id, created_at, post_id).\n- Follows indexed in BOTH directions.\n- FeedEntries keyed by (user_id, post_id),\n  queried by (user_id, published_at, post_id).\n- Redis keeps recent feed IDs; durable DB fallback.\n- Feed API merges normal + hot/public candidates,\n  then checks visibility and batch-hydrates content.\n- Object storage/CDN handles media, not private feeds.\n\nSCALE AND SAFETY\n- Shard recipient timelines by user_id if needed.\n- Cache, replicas, batch reads, bounded page sizes.\n- Rate limits + queue backpressure protect uptime.\n- Kafka at-least-once => idempotent workers.\n- Monitor p99, fan-out backlog, consumer lag,\n  cache hit rate, feed freshness and DB pressure.",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HIGH LEVEL DESIGN — CORRECTED\n\nSTORAGE AND CONSISTENCY\n- PostgreSQL source of truth for Posts + Follows.\n- Create post + outbox event in ONE DB transaction.\n- Outbox publisher retries sending to Kafka.\n- Timeline delivery is async / eventually consistent.\n- 99.99% availability is a target, not a DB switch.\n- Primary failover needs fencing; replicas may lag.\n- Backups / restore + multi-AZ replication matter.\n\nCAPACITY ESTIMATES (ASSUMPTIONS)\n- 100M DAU x 10 reads/day = 1B feed reads/day.\n  Average 11,574 RPS; 10x peak 115,741 RPS.\n- 10M posts/day = 116 write RPS; peak ~1,157.\n- 10M posts x 500 bytes = ~5 GB raw/day;\n  ~1.8 TB/year excluding indexes/replicas/media.\n- Full fan-out x 500 followers => 5B timeline\n  entry writes/day (~57.9k average writes/sec).\n\nSERVING PATH\n- Posts index by (author_id, created_at, post_id).\n- Follows indexed in BOTH directions.\n- FeedEntries keyed by (user_id, post_id),\n  queried by (user_id, published_at, post_id).\n- Redis keeps recent feed IDs; durable DB fallback.\n- Feed API merges normal + hot/public candidates,\n  then checks visibility and batch-hydrates content.\n- Object storage/CDN handles media, not private feeds.\n\nSCALE AND SAFETY\n- Shard recipient timelines by user_id if needed.\n- Cache, replicas, batch reads, bounded page sizes.\n- Rate limits + queue backpressure protect uptime.\n- Kafka at-least-once => idempotent workers.\n- Monitor p99, fan-out backlog, consumer lag,\n  cache hit rate, feed freshness and DB pressure.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xS6QUrm8kWWbhgXly8u-N",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2087.792851597155,
      "y": 1940.373244192296,
      "width": 820,
      "height": 1060,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b59",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 783726877,
      "version": 1185,
      "versionNonce": 1023102820,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794665975962,
      "created": 1794646416829,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "DEEP DIVE 1 — HYBRID FAN-OUT\n- Normal author: fan-out-on-WRITE to followers' FeedEntries.\n  Fast reads, but entry-write amplification.\n- Celebrity / hot author: fan-out-on-READ.\n  Store post once and merge into reader feed.\n- Inactive users: optionally lazy backfill on return.\n- Pick thresholds based on followers, user activity,\n  and fan-out queue capacity (not a magic number).\n\nDEEP DIVE 2 — CURSOR PAGINATION\n- ORDER BY created_at DESC, post_id DESC.\n- Cursor encodes last seen (created_at, post_id).\n- Use WHERE (created_at, post_id) < (:ts, :id)\n  for a chronological, stable feed source.\n- Fetch limit + 1; dedupe after merged sources.\n- Ranking can shift: use a snapshot/session cursor\n  or accept explicitly documented feed instability.\n\nDEEP DIVE 3 — EDGE CASES / IDEMPOTENCY\n- Unique Follows(follower_id, following_id).\n- Unique FeedEntries(user_id, post_id).\n- Client retries: idempotency key for create-post API.\n- Unfollow, delete, privacy change: filter on READ;\n  enqueue background removal / cache invalidation.\n- Follow behavior: define whether recent posts backfill.\n\nDEEP DIVE 4 — RELIABILITY / OPERATIONS\n- Write post + outbox in one atomic transaction.\n- Retry publisher; mark sent after broker ack.\n- Kafka consumer dedupes; replay; DLQ bad events.\n- Redis failure -> bounded fallback to DB.\n- Monitor p50/p95/p99 read/write latency,\n  feed-age, queue lag, dropped tasks and cache hits.",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "DEEP DIVE 1 — HYBRID FAN-OUT\n- Normal author: fan-out-on-WRITE to followers' FeedEntries.\n  Fast reads, but entry-write amplification.\n- Celebrity / hot author: fan-out-on-READ.\n  Store post once and merge into reader feed.\n- Inactive users: optionally lazy backfill on return.\n- Pick thresholds based on followers, user activity,\n  and fan-out queue capacity (not a magic number).\n\nDEEP DIVE 2 — CURSOR PAGINATION\n- ORDER BY created_at DESC, post_id DESC.\n- Cursor encodes last seen (created_at, post_id).\n- Use WHERE (created_at, post_id) < (:ts, :id)\n  for a chronological, stable feed source.\n- Fetch limit + 1; dedupe after merged sources.\n- Ranking can shift: use a snapshot/session cursor\n  or accept explicitly documented feed instability.\n\nDEEP DIVE 3 — EDGE CASES / IDEMPOTENCY\n- Unique Follows(follower_id, following_id).\n- Unique FeedEntries(user_id, post_id).\n- Client retries: idempotency key for create-post API.\n- Unfollow, delete, privacy change: filter on READ;\n  enqueue background removal / cache invalidation.\n- Follow behavior: define whether recent posts backfill.\n\nDEEP DIVE 4 — RELIABILITY / OPERATIONS\n- Write post + outbox in one atomic transaction.\n- Retry publisher; mark sent after broker ack.\n- Kafka consumer dedupes; replay; DLQ bad events.\n- Redis failure -> bounded fallback to DB.\n- Monitor p50/p95/p99 read/write latency,\n  feed-age, queue lag, dropped tasks and cache hits.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
