    },
    {
      "id": "HL1_sQ-VCjYeGUPr-KWHo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1966.119153344077,
      "y": 1969.5388902014324,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 975,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bA7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 199042012,
      "version": 1250,
      "versionNonce": 1225233252,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794734628470,
      "created": 1794733572002,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Approach we can used:\n1) Fixed Window Counter\n-> limit request couting based on timestamp\n-> like every 1 min only 10 req is allowed for user\ntradeoff : But may have req burst like 10:59,11.00, can have 20req in 2second.\n-> Most simple approach\n\n2) Sliding Window Log\n-> clever method using fixed windows with sliding window tech\n-> much better accuracy \ntradeoff: complexity to implement correctly\n\n3) Token Bucket(we choose this)\n-> think we have a bucket, holding a number of tokens.\n-> it is refilled at a constant rate, and will be used by user from request\n-> simple to implement\ntradeoff : how to choose correct bucket size and refill rate. cold start\n\nHow do we implement this?\nRedis\n1) req reach with userID\n2) gateway call redis to fetch current bucket state\n3) calculate and atomic update token usage to redis using LUA script\n4) makes decision to allow or block, if block return 429\n\nWhy Redis? Speed, Automatic cleanup(TTL), High availability(Redis clusters),\natomic operations(LUA)\n\nIf request exceed? return 429 Too many request or queue(but lead to more\nproblems)\nX-RateLimit-Limit: 100\nX-RateLimit-Remaining: 0\nX-RateLimit-Reset: 1640995200\nRetry-After: 60\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Approach we can used:\n1) Fixed Window Counter\n-> limit request couting based on timestamp\n-> like every 1 min only 10 req is allowed for user\ntradeoff : But may have req burst like 10:59,11.00, can have 20req in 2second.\n-> Most simple approach\n\n2) Sliding Window Log\n-> clever method using fixed windows with sliding window tech\n-> much better accuracy \ntradeoff: complexity to implement correctly\n\n3) Token Bucket(we choose this)\n-> think we have a bucket, holding a number of tokens.\n-> it is refilled at a constant rate, and will be used by user from request\n-> simple to implement\ntradeoff : how to choose correct bucket size and refill rate. cold start\n\nHow do we implement this?\nRedis\n1) req reach with userID\n2) gateway call redis to fetch current bucket state\n3) calculate and atomic update token usage to redis using LUA script\n4) makes decision to allow or block, if block return 429\n\nWhy Redis? Speed, Automatic cleanup(TTL), High availability(Redis clusters), atomic operations(LUA)\n\nIf request exceed? return 429 Too many request or queue(but lead to more problems)\nX-RateLimit-Limit: 100\nX-RateLimit-Remaining: 0\nX-RateLimit-Reset: 1640995200\nRetry-After: 60\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0nZoiX5PJIqrvobNupseH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1036.553066151672,
      "y": 1631.5577410266242,
      "width": 718.3195190429688,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bA8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1707950052,
      "version": 875,
      "versionNonce": 1503834460,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794733912303,
      "created": 1794733684833,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Where Rate limiter should put?\n\nAPI Gateway(We select)\n->every req hits the rate limiter first before reach service\n-> simple and strong protection.\ntradeoff : context is limited, only have ip address and jwt token.\nlike for specific user cannot get higher limits.\n\nGlobal Rate Limiting Service\n-> like another microservice to handle and decide.\n-> more flexibility, for specific users, and it maintains global\ntradeoff: latency, every request need to rpc call to this service first\n<10ms may cannot hit\n\nEach service having rate limiter build.\n-> fast since everything happens in memory\ntradeoff: each server dont know how many 1 user total request how much\nto the system, they only see their own side.\nGood for monolith\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Where Rate limiter should put?\n\nAPI Gateway(We select)\n->every req hits the rate limiter first before reach service\n-> simple and strong protection.\ntradeoff : context is limited, only have ip address and jwt token.\nlike for specific user cannot get higher limits.\n\nGlobal Rate Limiting Service\n-> like another microservice to handle and decide.\n-> more flexibility, for specific users, and it maintains global\ntradeoff: latency, every request need to rpc call to this service first\n<10ms may cannot hit\n\nEach service having rate limiter build.\n-> fast since everything happens in memory\ntradeoff: each server dont know how many 1 user total request how much\nto the system, they only see their own side.\nGood for monolith\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
