    {
      "id": "3qqdM-a0mWm-eRiJ5R1DI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1035.756922424061,
      "y": 2817.9594095897437,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 900,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1408638436,
      "version": 1358,
      "versionNonce": 936574948,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794735141575,
      "created": 1794734636042,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep Dive\n1) Scalability 1M RPS?\n-> redis sharding\n-> consistent hashing since more easy to add or remove redis instances.\n\n2) 99.99% Availability\nIf redis down?\n-> fail closed 503 Service Unavailable/429\ntradeoff : service down\n->fail open -> service still up\ntradeoff : heavy load to server may due do down server\n-> master-replica replication(like consensus)\ntradeoff : more infra cost.\n\n3) Minimize latency overhead\nNormally we need to do load test to monitor latency\n-> Instead of use TCP to redis, API gateway maintain a pool of persistent\nconnections.\n-> avoid TCP handshake overhead(20-50ms)\n-> geographic distribution -> multi zone\ntradeoff : more complexity\n\n4) hot keys\n-> Client side rate limiting\n-> req queing\n-> premium tiers having more rate limit\n-> automatic blocking\n-> DDoS Protection\n\n5) Dynamic RUle Configuration\n-> Push BAsed Configuration\n-> ZooKeeper maintains rules configrued and push to all connected clients.\n-> or using redis pub sub.\ntradeoff: more complexity, if have more api gateway? need to manage and\ncoordinate\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep Dive\n1) Scalability 1M RPS?\n-> redis sharding\n-> consistent hashing since more easy to add or remove redis instances.\n\n2) 99.99% Availability\nIf redis down?\n-> fail closed 503 Service Unavailable/429\ntradeoff : service down\n->fail open -> service still up\ntradeoff : heavy load to server may due do down server\n-> master-replica replication(like consensus)\ntradeoff : more infra cost.\n\n3) Minimize latency overhead\nNormally we need to do load test to monitor latency\n-> Instead of use TCP to redis, API gateway maintain a pool of persistent connections.\n-> avoid TCP handshake overhead(20-50ms)\n-> geographic distribution -> multi zone\ntradeoff : more complexity\n\n4) hot keys\n-> Client side rate limiting\n-> req queing\n-> premium tiers having more rate limit\n-> automatic blocking\n-> DDoS Protection\n\n5) Dynamic RUle Configuration\n-> Push BAsed Configuration\n-> ZooKeeper maintains rules configrued and push to all connected clients.\n-> or using redis pub sub.\ntradeoff: more complexity, if have more api gateway? need to manage and coordinate\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    }
  ],
